hat compromises Somalia’s security and stability. The two countries are working to ensure the security of international waterways and freedom of navigation. Follow Topics: Somalia Saudi Arabia R elated Riyadh’s King Khalid International Airport to reopen terminals on Sunday Grand Mosque head slams Houthi strikes on Makkah, Madinah as coalition defenses thwart attacks L atest updates Grand Mosque head slams Houthi strikes on Makkah, Madinah as coalition defenses thwart attacks Heavy thunderstorms to continue in parts of Saudi Arabia as October rains peak Israel says closing all land crossings with West Bank on election day Obama blasts Trump’s ‘chaos and cruelty’ while campaigning for Democrats Saudi lawmaker Saad Al-Otaibi takes helm of Arab Parliament Armed groups close Sweida-Damascus highway as US envoy voices concern L atest Updates Grand Mosque head slams Houthi strikes on Makkah, Madinah as coalition defenses thwart attacks Heavy thunderstorms to continue in parts of Saudi Arabia as October rains peak Saudi lawmaker Saad Al-Otaibi takes helm of Arab Parliament Riyadh’s King Khalid International Airport to reopen terminals on Sunday Saudi leaders send condolences to Jordan’s king over church attack Saudi Arabia Middle East World Business Sport Lifestyle Opinion Media Jobs Contact Us Advertise Privacy & Terms of Service Corporate and Sponsored Content © 2026 Arab News EMAIL ALERTS Stay on top of the issues that matter to you the most. Subscribe Now",
      "summary": "Somalia’s Prime Minister Hamza Abdi Barre arrived in Jeddah on October 24, 2026, where he was welcomed at King Abdulaziz International Airport by Jeddah Governor Prince Saud bin Abdullah bin Jalawi and other officials. This visit underscores the ongoing efforts to strengthen bilateral relations between Somalia and Saudi Arabia across various sectors. The Kingdom of Saudi Arabia has reiterated its support for Somalia's sovereignty and territorial integrity, emphasizing its commitment to rejecting any threats to Somalia’s security and stability. Both nations are collaborating to enhance the security of international waterways and ensure freedom of navigation, which is crucial for regional stability. This visit is part of a broader initiative to foster cooperation and mutual support between the two countries, reflecting their shared interests in maintaining peace and security in the region. The discussions during this visit are expected to pave the way for further diplomatic and economic engagements in the future.",
